{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-harness-seam-006-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/TestCommandSimulateSwitchClickTests.cs", "line": 673, "method": "ClearReason_MatchesThePatchPostfix", "category": "T3", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TestCommands/TestCommandSimulateSwitchClick.cs RefusedNoSwitchClearReason; change the constant's value -> red; change the patch's own literal at Source/Parsek/Patches/MapFocusObjectOnSelectPatch.cs:1064 -> stays green", "what_it_asserts": "TestCommandSimulateSwitchClick.RefusedNoSwitchClearReason equals the literal \"refused-no-switch\".", "why_weak": "The name claims byte-identity with the patch Postfix, but only one side is read. The Postfix clears with a bare string literal (MapFocusObjectOnSelectPatch.cs:1064, echoed in its log line at :1066), so changing the patch's spelling leaves this green and the one-grep-finds-both property silently gone.", "proposed_action": "Have MapFocusObjectOnSelectPatch's Postfix call ClearStockActionIntent with the shared constant instead of its own literal; then this pin covers both sides.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
